    "endingForgiveness": "The recoil-to-wallbounce transfer has clean early and late variants and lands on an eleven-tile one-way rest. Missing it drops to a safe local floor beside the reusable recoil plate. From that rest onward, the return is a climb, a broad upper shelf and an ordinary jump to the twelve-tile entrance balcony. A three-second pause on the middle return shelf remains valid.",
    "entrance": "Upper-west overlook with the closed exit visible.",
    "exit": "The same overlook after circling below and returning over the restored central pier.",
    "interconnection": "The knight must really visit the middle pressure shelf before Oren can replay that path and hold it. The helper opens the central pier for the outward lower crossing, then must leave the same plate to restore it as the recoil-assisted return wall. The restored pier also supports the upper return across the same room to the original entrance gate.",
    "designNotes": "64\u00d748 tiles (3.34 normal screen areas), with upper overlook, middle companion shelf, lower gallery and an upper return through the same central structure. No hidden action receipts gate the exit. The single east tally opens real gates; Oren\u2019s pressure and the central pier retain their ordinary device behavior. The far-east outer wall has visible inward teeth and no intermediate shelf, so it cannot replace the central return pier."
